sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor K as Kunde
    participant FM as ForgotPasswordModel
    participant RC as IRecaptchaVerifier
    participant US as IUserAccountStore
    participant PL as IPendingLoginStore
    participant ES as IEmailSender
    participant RM as ResetPasswordModel
    participant LO as LoginLockoutTracker

    K->>FM: POST /Account/ForgotPassword (email, captcha token)
    Note over FM: [EnableRateLimiting("auth")]
    FM->>RC: VerifyAsync(captcha token)
    alt captcha rejected
        FM-->>K: "Bekraeft at du ikke er en robot"
    else captcha ok
        FM->>US: FindByEmail(email)

        alt account exists and is active
            US-->>FM: ApplicationUser
            FM->>PL: Create(userId, null, 15 min)
            PL-->>FM: raw token (SHA-256 hash stored)
            FM->>ES: SendAsync(reset link) - Danish or English, after the browser
        else no such account, or inactive
            US-->>FM: null
            Note over FM: Nothing is sent - and nothing<br/>in the response says so.
        end

        FM-->>K: Redirect to /Account/CheckEmail?purpose=reset
        Note over FM,K: Identical response either way.<br/>Otherwise the form becomes a way to test<br/>which email addresses are registered.
    end

    K->>RM: GET /Account/ResetPassword?token=...
    RM->>PL: IsValid(token)
    Note over RM,PL: Peek only. The token is not spent here,<br/>so sitting on the form for a while<br/>does not invalidate it.
    alt token missing or expired
        RM-->>K: "Linket er udlobet"
    else token valid
        RM-->>K: new-password form

        K->>RM: POST (new password, confirm)
        RM->>PL: IsValid(token) again
        RM->>RM: validate ModelState (min 8 characters, must match)
        RM->>PL: Consume(token)
        Note over PL: Spent here, at the point of use.<br/>Single redemption.
        alt token already used or account gone
            RM-->>K: "Linket er udlobet"
        else ok
            RM->>RM: PasswordHasher.HashPassword
            RM->>US: UpdatePassword(userId, hash)
            Note over RM,US: The same UPDATE replaces Users.SecurityStamp:<br/>every session signed in with the old password -<br/>a stolen cookie included - ends on its next request.
            RM->>LO: Clear(email)
            Note over RM,LO: The only thing that lifts a hard lockout<br/>(5 failed attempts).
            RM->>ES: SendAsync("Din adgangskode er aendret"<br/>or "Your password has been changed")
            Note over RM,ES: ASVS 2.5.5 - every change to a sign-in factor<br/>is notified to the account owner.
            RM-->>K: Redirect to /Account/Login with toast
        end
    end
